Let me also explain why this beats a plain Mutex:
- A plain Mutex around sequential_work would still serialize, but every consumer would block on the mutex, and the holder would process only ONE job per lock acquisition unless it loops. The contenders mechanism lets the holder drain continuously AND avoids waking/blocking overhead — losers return immediately without waiting. It's essentially a "lock with elimination": concurrent consume calls are resolved atomically, only one proceeds, and it stays as long as there's work.

